Priority: P0
Title:    [P0] Remediate /usr/lib64/httpd/modules/libphp.so (VULNERABLE, SAPI: apache2handler)
Steps:
  1. No verified Rocky fix is recorded yet; check vendor security trackers for backported package updates.
  2. Temporary configuration mitigation (applies to CVE-2026-109619 only; not a fix):
     Create drop-in INI file /etc/php/conf.d/99-mitigation.ini:
       session.upload_progress.enabled = 0
       fatal_error_backtraces = 0
     Alternatively, in Apache configuration:
       php_admin_flag session.upload_progress.enabled off
       php_admin_value fatal_error_backtraces 0
Commands:
  [Upgrade RPM PHP packages] dnf check-update; dnf upgrade php-cli php-fpm php-common
Restart Hints:
  - reload Apache (e.g. systemctl reload httpd)
Notes:    WARNING: A configuration mitigation is a temporary risk reduction only and is NOT a fix. CVE-2026-109618 has no known configuration mitigation; upgrading PHP is required.
